1
00:01:23,107 --> 00:01:30,943
When Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه was feeling, death approaching him

2
00:01:33,564 --> 00:01:37,635
he told the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم,

3
00:01:39,990 --> 00:01:46,222
I want you, to choose for yourselves a Khalifah(خليفه) after me

4
00:01:48,515 --> 00:01:52,653
your Baiy’ah(بيعة) to me is over, and I am not incharge of your affairs anymore

5
00:01:53,647 --> 00:01:55,747
because I am leaving this Duniyah(دُنِيَّا).

6
00:01:59,676 --> 00:02:02,493
And he wanted this affair to be settled before he dies.

7
00:02:05,902 --> 00:02:08,537
So, Sahabah رضي الله عنهم discussed the matter

8
00:02:10,661 --> 00:02:12,655
but then they came back to Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) and they said:

9
00:02:12,750 --> 00:02:20,949
We trust your advice, so we put it back in your hands you choose for us.

10
00:02:24,652 --> 00:02:28,354
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said: Then give me some time to decide.

11
00:02:34,853 --> 00:02:40,851
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه called Abdur Rahman Ibn Awf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف)

12
00:02:44,569 --> 00:02:50,030
and he asked him, he said: "Inform me about Umar(عُمَر)?"

13
00:02:53,053 --> 00:02:55,203
Abdur Rahman Ibn Awf رضي الله عنه said:

14
00:02:55,294 --> 00:03:01,255
"You don’t ask me about anything but you have better knowledge than me."

15
00:03:03,507 --> 00:03:07,833
Anything that you ask me about, you know it better than I do.

16
00:03:10,214 --> 00:03:15,588
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said: "Even though, I want to hear your opinion?"

17
00:03:17,605 --> 00:03:19,246
So, Abdur Rahman Ibn Awf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف) Said:

18
00:03:20,884 --> 00:03:23,634
هُوَ خَيْرًا مِمَّا تَظُنْ

19
00:03:24,068 --> 00:03:26,483
Umar(عُمَر) is better than what you think of him!

20
00:03:32,225 --> 00:03:33,793
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه said:

21
00:03:33,817 --> 00:03:34,610
اُكْتُمْ عَنِّيْ

22
00:03:34,757 --> 00:03:38,877
Keep this conversation private, he left.

23
00:03:40,257 --> 00:03:42,550
And then Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) invited Uthman Ibn Affan( عثمان ابن عفان),

24
00:03:44,114 --> 00:03:46,549
he said: "Tell me about Umar(عُمَر)?"

25
00:03:47,709 --> 00:03:50,373
Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) said: You know him

26
00:03:51,075 --> 00:03:53,162
basically he said the same thing,

27
00:03:53,943 --> 00:03:56,899
"Anything you ask me about, you know it better than I do!"

28
00:03:57,383 --> 00:04:04,435
The Sahabah رضي الله عنهم  gave it to Abu Bakr(ابو بكر), that he was most scholarly and knowledgeable among them.

29
00:04:06,850 --> 00:04:12,408
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) said: I still want to hear your opinion on Umar(عُمَر),

30
00:04:13,670 --> 00:04:26,229
he said: I know what I know of Umar(عُمَر), and Allah is my witness.

31
00:04:27,211 --> 00:04:34,984
Is that, his inside is better than his outside and there is none among us, like him.

32
00:04:37,263 --> 00:04:39,331
There is none of us equal to Umar(عُمَر)

33
00:04:40,355 --> 00:04:44,855
and what we see of Umar(عُمَر) in the outside and think is good and what is inside is even better.

34
00:04:51,817 --> 00:04:54,831
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه told Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان),

35
00:04:55,858 --> 00:05:00,444
"If I am going to by pass him, it's not going beyond you!"

36
00:05:02,114 --> 00:05:05,848
If I am not going to choose Umar(عُمَر), you will be my next choice.

37
00:05:10,967 --> 00:05:14,362
And then he make Naseeha(نصيحه) with some of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم

38
00:05:14,667 --> 00:05:17,272
for example, Usayed Ibn Khuzair(اُسَيْد اِبن خضير), one of Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار).

39
00:05:18,318 --> 00:05:20,892
He was asked about Umar(عُمَر).

40
00:05:21,516 --> 00:05:25,428
Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه asked him, Usayed Ibn Khuzair(اُسَيْد اِبن خضير) said:

41
00:05:27,796 --> 00:05:29,041
يَرْضَى الِلرِّضَا

42
00:05:29,446 --> 00:05:32,134
"He is pleased, with what pleases the ummah(امة),

43
00:05:32,769 --> 00:05:35,853
and he is displeased with what displeases the Ummah(امة).

44
00:05:36,556 --> 00:05:42,948
And there is none among us, who is more competent, stronger for this affair, then him.

45
00:05:44,299 --> 00:05:47,681
He is the most competent among us, to run this affair.

46
00:05:51,355 --> 00:05:55,703
So, basically all of the Sahabah(صحابه) were giving Umar(عُمَر), the same council

47
00:05:58,668 --> 00:06:04,236
but there was the concern of some of the Sahabah(صحابه) for example, Talha(طلحه)

48
00:06:04,828 --> 00:06:07,060
that Umar(عُمَر) is rough

49
00:06:09,256 --> 00:06:15,160
and Talha(طلحه) was quite stern in the Naseeha(نصيحه) that he gave Abu Bakr(ابو بكر)

50
00:06:15,579 --> 00:06:21,446
he told him, O Abu Bakr(ابو بكر)! How will you answer Allah on the Day of Judgment?

51
00:06:23,284 --> 00:06:30,589
When He tells you, you appointed over the Muslims a man, who is harsh and rough.

52
00:06:33,905 --> 00:06:41,065
Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابوبكرالصديق) was ill and he was on his bed and he sat up straight and he said:

53
00:06:41,089 --> 00:06:42,796
اَبِالله تُخَوِّفُوْنِيْ ؟

54
00:06:43,579 --> 00:06:45,177
Are you threatening me with Allah?

55
00:06:45,903 --> 00:06:51,646
I will respond to Allah on the Day of Judgment by saying; "I have chosen the best among them to lead them.

56
00:06:53,363 --> 00:06:54,555
he is the best among you.

57
00:06:58,625 --> 00:07:03,099
So, the opinion of Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was settling on Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه

58
00:07:05,069 --> 00:07:11,899
and he wrote a document of his appointment of Umar(عُمَر).

59
00:07:12,510 --> 00:07:14,860
And he gave that document to Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان)

60
00:07:15,201 --> 00:07:19,860
and he said: "You go and read it in the Masjid(مسجد) and you take a Baiy’ah(بيعة) from the people."

61
00:07:20,269 --> 00:07:23,898
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) wanted to make sure that this issue is settled before he dies.

62
00:07:24,557 --> 00:07:27,393
So, Uthman(عثمان) goes to the Masjid(مسجد) and, he tells the people,

63
00:07:27,631 --> 00:07:31,506
Do you give Baiy’ah(بيعة) to, who is in this document? And they all gave Baiy’ah(بيعة)."

64
00:07:32,034 --> 00:07:37,327
So, Baiy’ah(بيعة) was given to Umar(عُمَر) during the time of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه before he passes away.

65
00:07:47,763 --> 00:07:50,389
Ibn Masood رضي الله عنه, he says;

66
00:07:50,413 --> 00:07:52,516
أَفْرَسُ النَّاسِ ثَلَاثَةْ ؛

67
00:07:54,472 --> 00:07:58,648
وَصَاحِبَةِ مُوْسى حِيْنَ قَالَتْ: يَا أَبَتِ اسْتَأْجِرْهُ

68
00:07:59,116 --> 00:08:02,177
إِنَّ خَيْرَ مَنِ اسْتَأْجَرْتَ الْقَوِيُّ الْأَمِينُ

69
00:08:03,372 --> 00:08:11,940
وَصَاحِبْ يُوْسُفْ حِيْنَ قَال :أَكْرِمِي مَثْوَاهُ عَسَىٰ أَنْ يَنْفَعَنَا أَوْ نَتَّخِذَهُ وَلَدًا

70
00:08:12,777 --> 00:08:16,711
وَأَبُوْ بَكَرْ حِيْنَ اَسْتَخْلَفَ عُمر

71
00:08:18,128 --> 00:08:38,940
Ibn Masood(ابن مسعود) says; "The three with the greatest intuitions among mankind are the woman or the wife of Musa(موسى)

72
00:08:40,098 --> 00:08:45,254
 and the Master of Yousuf(يوسف) and Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابو بكر الصديق), when he appointed Umar(عمر).

73
00:08:46,784 --> 00:08:48,022
What are these three incidence?

74
00:08:48,062 --> 00:08:49,705
Ibn Masood(ابن مسعود) is saying,

75
00:08:49,973 --> 00:08:57,344
that these three have the greatest Farasah(فراسة), intuition that ever existed among humanity.

76
00:08:59,116 --> 00:09:00,232
The wife of Musa(موسى),

77
00:09:02,601 --> 00:09:04,521
when Musaعليه السلام left Egypt,

78
00:09:05,787 --> 00:09:09,751
he was running away from the Egypt to save his life

79
00:09:10,410 --> 00:09:14,944
that was before he became a Nabi(نَبِي) because they wanted to execute him,

80
00:09:16,066 --> 00:09:18,614
so he left Egypt and he went to the land of Mad'yan(مدائن),

81
00:09:20,173 --> 00:09:25,937
he left alone and he didn’t have any transportation

82
00:09:27,130 --> 00:09:31,574
and he was travelling and his shoes were torn apart,

83
00:09:31,665 --> 00:09:37,173
and then his skin on his feet was tearing apart

84
00:09:38,444 --> 00:09:43,392
and he was so hungry he had to eat the leaves of trees

85
00:09:43,911 --> 00:09:48,319
until, his lips were cracking and the color was turning green.

86
00:09:48,681 --> 00:09:51,781
Because these are not edible, they not suitable for human consumption.

87
00:09:53,869 --> 00:09:58,637
And Musa عليه السلام is going through that difficult journey

88
00:10:00,457 --> 00:10:02,478
and then he reaches to the land of Mad'yan(مدائن)

89
00:10:04,363 --> 00:10:07,951
and even though he is exhausted and tired and hungry.

90
00:10:08,934 --> 00:10:13,861
He sees these two women waiting on the side of this well,

91
00:10:14,125 --> 00:10:16,397
while all are the men are fighting to get water.

92
00:10:18,303 --> 00:10:20,393
Musa عليه السلام is still practicing,

93
00:10:20,545 --> 00:10:22,645
 اَمَرْ بِالْمَعْرُوْفَ وَ نَهِيْ عَنِ الْمُنْكَرَْ

94
00:10:22,738 --> 00:10:24,780
Even though, he is in that exhausted state

95
00:10:26,303 --> 00:10:30,516
This was the personality of Musa(موسى) he cannot hold back

96
00:10:31,485 --> 00:10:33,585
"enjoining good and forbidding evil"

97
00:10:34,129 --> 00:10:37,824
even if he is extremely tired and exhausted.

98
00:10:38,158 --> 00:10:41,531
He is in a foreign land he doesn’t know anybody there

99
00:10:41,840 --> 00:10:46,520
but he still cannot stand seeing wrong happening in front of his eyes.

100
00:10:49,192 --> 00:10:52,169
So, he goes in and asks these women,

101
00:10:52,218 --> 00:10:59,894
these two women, they're sisters that how come you are not quenching the thirst of your animals?

102
00:11:01,697 --> 00:11:05,884
They said: We cannot go in and fight with the men.

103
00:11:07,237 --> 00:11:11,521
These men had no honor, they're fighting over the water

104
00:11:11,539 --> 00:11:14,329
and have these women waiting, they are not standing in queue

105
00:11:14,653 --> 00:11:19,167
They're just fighting to get the water and the poor ladies are waiting.

106
00:11:20,011 --> 00:11:27,171
Musa عليه السلام jumps in and fights his way through, and he gets them water.

107
00:11:28,359 --> 00:11:32,863
And he's even fighting, when he's in that exhausted state, he gets some water

108
00:11:33,616 --> 00:11:39,441
and then he goes under a tree and he throws himself under the tree, completely exhausted.

109
00:11:41,160 --> 00:11:46,525
He has no where to stay, no food to eat, no supporter no helper.

110
00:11:47,388 --> 00:11:50,288
So, he just lays down, and he says

111
00:11:50,350 --> 00:11:54,216
رَبِّ إِنِّي لِمَا أَنْزَلْتَ إِلَيَّ مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَقِيرٌ

112
00:11:54,766 --> 00:12:01,143
"O Allah whatever good, you bring down on me, I need it."

113
00:12:02,862 --> 00:12:08,807
I have reached, a state where anything would do, O Allah! Anything,

114
00:12:09,712 --> 00:12:13,025
رَبِّ إِنِّي لِمَا أَنْزَلْتَ إِلَيَّ مِنْ خَيْرٍ فَقِيرٌ

115
00:12:13,386 --> 00:12:15,082
He is begging Allahعَزّ وجَلّ for anything.

116
00:12:17,895 --> 00:12:21,193
Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) the Dua(دُعَا) of Musa(موسى) was immediately accepted.

117
00:12:22,419 --> 00:12:28,221
And this tells you brothers and sisters, the consequences of doing good.

118
00:12:30,293 --> 00:12:33,923
Musa عليه السلام has every excuse in the world to be passive at that moment.

119
00:12:34,036 --> 00:12:37,337
And just sit down under the tree and forget about what those people are doing?

120
00:12:41,503 --> 00:12:46,958
Those two women they went back home, and one of them went to her father and said:

121
00:12:46,982 --> 00:12:49,589
O my father! Why don’t you hire that man?

122
00:12:49,686 --> 00:12:52,894
Because the best man to hire is the man, who is trust worthy and strong.

123
00:12:54,523 --> 00:13:00,161
That action of Musa(موسى), that action of Musa(موسى) look at the consequences of it.

124
00:13:00,800 --> 00:13:04,704
The woman goes back home and tells her old father, hire this man.

125
00:13:05,565 --> 00:13:08,984
So, she comes back and she calls Musa(موسى).

126
00:13:09,319 --> 00:13:11,818
Musa(موسى) goes there and he gets a job,

127
00:13:12,933 --> 00:13:15,341
he finds a wife because this woman marries him.

128
00:13:17,556 --> 00:13:25,601
and he was given a guarantee of work up to eight or ten years.

129
00:13:27,303 --> 00:13:31,482
So, he signed a contract to work for this man for eight to ten years

130
00:13:34,270 --> 00:13:38,198
as a result of that small action of good that he did

131
00:13:38,279 --> 00:13:40,181
لَا تَحْقِرَنَّ مِنَ الْمَعْرُوْفِ شَيْئًا

132
00:13:40,206 --> 00:13:43,897
Rasool Allah ﷺ says; "Never belittle anything good that you do." Anything!

133
00:13:44,476 --> 00:13:49,064
You don’t know what will be the act that will make it or break it.

134
00:13:49,550 --> 00:13:51,387
Whether on the side of good or side of evil.

135
00:13:53,674 --> 00:13:57,207
A person could go up levels in Jannah(جنة) because of one good word

136
00:13:57,518 --> 00:14:00,568
and they good go down levels in Hell fire because of one evil word.

137
00:14:01,692 --> 00:14:03,692
And they're not even paying attention to those words.

138
00:14:05,202 --> 00:14:10,490
One small deed can tilt the scales and you will enter into Jannah(جنة)

139
00:14:10,796 --> 00:14:15,146
one evil deed can tilt the scales and you end up going to Hell fire.

140
00:14:16,117 --> 00:14:18,017
لَا تَحْقِرَنَّ مِنَ الْمَعْرُوْفِ شَيْئًا

141
00:14:18,302 --> 00:14:20,231
"Do not belittle anything good that you do."

142
00:14:20,791 --> 00:14:23,959
And in the same time, don't see any sin as being insignificant

143
00:14:25,996 --> 00:14:31,800
So, Ibn Masood(ابن مسعود) says; This woman had great Farasa(فراسه), is very intuitive.

144
00:14:32,891 --> 00:14:34,560
THE SECOND SAHIB YUSUF(صاحب يوسُف):

145
00:14:36,709 --> 00:14:41,399
When Yusuf(يوسف) was found in the well, he was sold as a slave in Egypt.

146
00:14:42,071 --> 00:14:48,479
The man, who purchased him, we would say the Prime Minister or Treasurer of Egypt

147
00:14:49,070 --> 00:14:50,741
He is the one who, purchased Yusuf(يوسف),

148
00:14:51,291 --> 00:14:55,055
when he took this young boy home, he told his wife:

149
00:14:55,661 --> 00:14:56,798
اَكْرِمِيْ مَثْوَاهْ

150
00:14:58,091 --> 00:15:00,239
Make his stay with us honorable.

151
00:15:00,752 --> 00:15:05,360
He is a slave, but he told his wife make his stay among us all honorable

152
00:15:05,884 --> 00:15:13,192
because one day, he might be of great benefit for us or we might adopt him as a son.

153
00:15:14,204 --> 00:15:22,004
So, this man saw some marks of intelligence and wisdom in Yusuf عليه السلام

154
00:15:22,333 --> 00:15:26,028
so he gave special instructions to his wife to treat him well.

155
00:15:28,623 --> 00:15:31,596
He didn’t know that one day this man will grow up and be one of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء).

156
00:15:34,035 --> 00:15:34,973
AND THE THIRD:

157
00:15:35,924 --> 00:15:39,730
Ibn Masood(ابن مسعود) says; Abu Bakr(ابو بكر), when he appointed Umar(عُمَر) to be the Khalifah(خليفه).

158
00:15:40,791 --> 00:15:44,108
May be one of the greatest deeds of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه is

159
00:15:44,148 --> 00:15:48,038
that before he died, he appointed Umar(عُمَر) to be the Khalifah(خليفه).

160
00:15:49,034 --> 00:15:54,646
Because everything that Umar(عُمَر) did after that, goes into the scales of Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابو بكر الصديق).

161
00:15:56,826 --> 00:16:00,344
And that’s why Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابو بكر الصديق) is higher than everybody including Umar(عُمَر)

162
00:16:00,867 --> 00:16:06,409
because Umar(عُمَر) his Khilafah(خِلَافَه) becomes one of the Hasanat(حسنات) of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

163
00:16:09,031 --> 00:16:12,073
It was a choice that had a Toufique(توفيق) of Allahعَزّ وجَلّ

164
00:16:12,097 --> 00:16:20,803
Allahعَزّ وجَلّ gave Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) success in that choice of leaving behind Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه.

165
00:16:25,939 --> 00:16:30,918
Ibn Abbas رضي الله عنه when Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was passing away

166
00:16:31,402 --> 00:16:42,550
he came and he gave him, some words to comfort the Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه

167
00:16:43,340 --> 00:16:44,905
among those words he said;

168
00:16:44,930 --> 00:16:49,627
وَلَمْ يَخْتَلِفْ عَلى خِلَافَتِكَ اَثْنَانْ

169
00:16:51,322 --> 00:16:54,811
No two men disputed, your Khilafah(خِلَافَه)

170
00:16:56,064 --> 00:16:59,637
which means that the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) of Umar(عُمَر) was the consensus of the Sahabah(صحابه)

171
00:17:00,849 --> 00:17:06,734
and we know that consensus, in this Ummah(امة) is Hujjah(حجة), is an evidence

172
00:17:07,828 --> 00:17:09,848
and here we just don’t have consensus of the Ummah(امة),

173
00:17:09,872 --> 00:17:13,869
we have consensus of Greatest Generation of the Ummah(امة), the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم.

174
00:17:15,341 --> 00:17:19,520
We know in Fiqh(فقه) that the evidence is the Ayah(آية) of the Qur’an

175
00:17:19,857 --> 00:17:23,748
or the Hadith(حديث) of Rasool Allah ﷺ or Ijma’ah(اجماع), the consensus.

176
00:17:24,438 --> 00:17:29,857
So, it was the consensus of Sahabah رضي الله عنهم that the Umar(عُمَر) is the Khalifah(خليفه)

177
00:17:31,301 --> 00:17:34,401
and that he is the most deserving of that position.

178
00:17:35,189 --> 00:17:42,657
So, who can dare, after that to doubt in the validity of the Khilafah(خِلَافَه) of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه?

179
00:17:43,897 --> 00:17:49,538
Among the generations, where there's evil and Bida’a(بدعة).

180
00:17:50,615 --> 00:17:55,223
If the greatest generation, the pure generation of the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم agreed

181
00:17:55,838 --> 00:17:57,843
that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) is the Khalifah(خليفه),

182
00:17:58,616 --> 00:18:02,770
who can dare to say after that no it should have been somebody else?

183
00:18:10,801 --> 00:18:13,971
When Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه became Khalifah(خليفه)

184
00:18:14,570 --> 00:18:22,464
there are few different speeches, that were attributed to him, one of them was, he says;

185
00:18:22,589 --> 00:18:26,473
ثُمَّ إِنِّيْ قَدْ وُلِّيْتُ أمُوْرَكُمْ أَيُّهَا النَّاسْ

186
00:18:27,532 --> 00:18:34,412
"O people! Know that I have been appointed to govern your affairs"

187
00:18:35,594 --> 00:18:39,128
فَاعْلَمُوْا أَنَّ تِلْكَ الشِّدَّةْ قَدْ أُضْعِفَتْ

188
00:18:40,448 --> 00:18:46,928
So realize now, that my roughness is now weaker,

189
00:18:47,965 --> 00:18:50,330
that roughness has been weakened.

190
00:18:51,446 --> 00:18:55,013
وَلَا كِنَّهَا إِنَّمَا تَكُوْنُ عَلى  أَهْلِ الظُّلْمِ وَالتَّعَدِّيْ

191
00:18:55,904 --> 00:19:02,770
But I will still be rough and harsh on the people of oppression and transgression.

192
00:19:06,632 --> 00:19:13,205
وَلَسْتُ أَدَعْ أَحَدًا يَظْلِمُ أَحَدًا َ أَوْ يَتَعَدَّى عِلَيْهِ حَتَّى أَضَعَ خَدَّه’ عَلَى الْاَرْضَ،

193
00:19:13,629 --> 00:19:17,729
وَأَضَعُ قَدَمِيْ عَلَى الْخَدِّالْآخَرْ حَتَّى يُذْعِنِ الْحَقّّ

194
00:19:19,471 --> 00:19:21,999
"And I am not going to see anybody who oppresses others,

195
00:19:22,330 --> 00:19:27,730
but I am going to put one of their cheeks in the dirt

196
00:19:28,080 --> 00:19:30,216
and I will step with my foot over the other cheek,

197
00:19:30,659 --> 00:19:34,131
until they give the people what is due to them.

198
00:19:37,140 --> 00:19:37,749
And then he said:

199
00:19:37,773 --> 00:19:43,755
وَاِنِّيْ بَعْدَ شِدَّتِيْ تِلْكَ اَضْعُ  خَدِّيْ  عَلَى الْاَرْضْ، لِأَهْلِ الْعَفَافِ وَالْكَفَافْ

200
00:19:43,779 --> 00:19:49,770
"But I will put my cheek, on the floor to the people of piety and  righteousness. "

201
00:19:50,885 --> 00:19:57,380
I will be so humble towards these people, it is as if, I am placing my cheek on the earth for them.

202
00:19:59,585 --> 00:20:05,239
وَلَكُمْ عَلَيَّ أَيُّهَا النَّاسْ، خِصَالْ أَذْكُرُوْهَالَكُمْ فَخُذُوْنِيْ بِهَا

203
00:20:05,676 --> 00:20:09,604
And I will promise you a few things which you can hold me accountable to.

204
00:20:11,799 --> 00:20:19,151
لَكُمْ عَلَيَّ أَلَّاْ اَجْتَبِيْ شَيْئًا مِنْ خَرَاجِكُمْ وَلَا مِمَّا أَفَاءَ الله عَلَيْكُمْ إِلَّا مِنْ وَجْهِهْ

205
00:20:19,552 --> 00:20:22,310
"I promise you that I will take nothing of your Kharaj(خراج),

206
00:20:22,551 --> 00:20:24,509
Kharaj(خراج) is what your land produces.

207
00:20:25,033 --> 00:20:26,552
وَلَا مِمَّا أَفَاءَ الله عَلَيْكُمْ

208
00:20:26,576 --> 00:20:30,080
And I will take nothing from the spoils of war, that you get

209
00:20:31,187 --> 00:20:34,765
except that which is rightfully taken.

210
00:20:35,289 --> 00:20:38,789
Which I am allowed to take, according to the Book of Allah

211
00:20:41,376 --> 00:20:43,382
وَلَكُمْ عَلَيَّ أَنْ أَزِيْدَهْ

212
00:20:43,406 --> 00:20:48,581
Then he also said: And that money I will only spend it, in accordance to law of Allah.

213
00:20:48,816 --> 00:20:51,524
So, I will not going to take anything except if the Book of Allah allows it,

214
00:20:51,748 --> 00:20:54,448
and I will only spend it, in a way that pleases Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

215
00:20:56,994 --> 00:21:07,902
وَلَكُمْ عَلَيَّ أَنْ أَزِيْدَ عَطَايَاكُمْ وَأَرْزَاقَكُمْ اِنْشَآءَ الله تَعَالى وَأَسُدَّا ثُغُوْرَكُمْ

216
00:21:08,723 --> 00:21:14,190
And I promise you that I will increase your salaries, and your provisions

217
00:21:14,964 --> 00:21:18,532
and I promise you that I will protect your borders."

218
00:21:20,719 --> 00:21:23,262
وَلَكُمْ عَلَيَّ أَلَّا أُلْقٍيْكُمْ فِى الْمَهَالِكْ

219
00:21:24,448 --> 00:21:27,431
"And I promise you not to throw you into destruction."

220
00:21:27,801 --> 00:21:28,806
وَلَا أُجْمِرُكُمْ

221
00:21:29,214 --> 00:21:34,573
"And I will not keep the soldiers away from their families, for extended periods of time."

222
00:21:36,299 --> 00:21:42,095
وَإِذَا غِبْتُمْ فِى الْبُعُوْثِ فَأَنَا أَبُوا الْعِيَالْ حَتَّى تَرْجِعُوْ اِلِيْهِمْ

223
00:21:42,708 --> 00:21:49,014
And when I send you out in Jihad(جهاد) I will be the father of your children, until you come back.

224
00:21:49,973 --> 00:21:52,399
So, have Taqwa(تقوي), O servants of Allah!"

225
00:21:54,206 --> 00:21:57,878
A FEW POINTS REGARDING THIS SPEECH

226
00:21:58,462 --> 00:22:01,829
First of all Umar(عُمَر) is changing his personality

227
00:22:02,982 --> 00:22:08,308
Umar(عُمَر) is saying, that roughness is now turning into softness.

228
00:22:10,014 --> 00:22:15,912
Abu Bakr As-Siddiqueرضي الله عنه has said, when some of the Sahabah(صحابه) told him;

229
00:22:15,983 --> 00:22:18,383
How will you appoint a man, who is tough?

230
00:22:19,054 --> 00:22:24,372
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) said: Umar(عُمَر) was tough, because he saw that I was weak

231
00:22:25,686 --> 00:22:30,904
but when I pass away, he will leave behind much of that behavior

232
00:22:32,939 --> 00:22:35,327
And Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said about himself,

233
00:22:36,657 --> 00:22:44,823
Rasool Allah ﷺ had a very great heart that was open for everyone

234
00:22:45,834 --> 00:22:48,634
so I had to be a sword in his presence.

235
00:22:50,649 --> 00:22:56,477
And Abu Bakr As-Siddique(ابو بكر الصديق) was very soft man, so I had to be tough in his presence.

236
00:22:57,561 --> 00:23:03,748
But now, since I have assumed responsibility of you,

237
00:23:04,589 --> 00:23:07,189
that harshness will be turned into softness.

238
00:23:08,525 --> 00:23:10,427
It shows you something about Umar(عُمَر)

239
00:23:11,816 --> 00:23:16,885
that he had control over himself to the extent that he can change his personality.

240
00:23:18,995 --> 00:23:26,133
And he could be the man of the moment and act according to, what those times need.

241
00:23:27,764 --> 00:23:33,004
So, in the times of Rasool Allah ﷺ he was carrying the certain character,

242
00:23:33,028 --> 00:23:38,696
in times of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) a certain character, and in the time of his Khilafah(خِلَافَه), he change his ways

243
00:23:39,546 --> 00:23:45,184
So, that he could modify his personality to be appropriate for those circumstances

244
00:23:46,212 --> 00:23:52,054
And this is great ability, don’t be a slave of yourself.

245
00:23:53,347 --> 00:23:58,795
You need to take control of yourself and you need to tame your Nafs(نفس).

246
00:24:01,791 --> 00:24:08,329
Number two: You can see the importance of financial justice.

247
00:24:10,338 --> 00:24:14,394
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is saying that I am not going to take your money, and I am not going to spend your money,

248
00:24:14,805 --> 00:24:16,372
except in the rightful way.

249
00:24:17,821 --> 00:24:23,539
A Muslim leader is not a Muslim leader if he is taking money in an un rightful way, and spending it in a wrong way.

250
00:24:25,086 --> 00:24:31,698
Part of being an Ameer(امير) over Muslims is that you are accountable financially

251
00:24:32,003 --> 00:24:37,621
 and you spend the money and you take it way, in a way that pleases Allahعَزّوجَلّ

252
00:24:38,978 --> 00:24:43,954
So Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) is mentioning this as one of the points that people need to hold him accountable to.

253
00:24:47,456 --> 00:24:51,219
Number three: What an amazing government was that

254
00:24:53,184 --> 00:24:57,398
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) is paying, his citizens salaries

255
00:24:59,632 --> 00:25:02,273
and this is not for any work that they are doing.

256
00:25:02,999 --> 00:25:08,757
Every citizen of the Islamic Khilafah(خِلَافَه) would get a salary, a payment.

257
00:25:11,801 --> 00:25:21,169
These were not government employees, everyone has a right to money of the Islamic Treasury.

258
00:25:21,907 --> 00:25:23,912
This is money that belongs to the Muslims,

259
00:25:24,115 --> 00:25:26,829
so Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was giving it back to them.

260
00:25:27,771 --> 00:25:32,125
This is not something that, he invented this is something that existed in times of Abu Bakr(ابو بكر)

261
00:25:32,272 --> 00:25:34,114
and in the times of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

262
00:25:34,245 --> 00:25:35,951
 Umar(عُمَر) just promised to increase it.

263
00:25:36,346 --> 00:25:37,983
I am going to increase your payments.

264
00:25:39,935 --> 00:25:41,435
So, those were very blessed times.

265
00:25:44,237 --> 00:25:49,626
Number four: In offensive Jihad(جهاد), the safety of the Muslims is paramount

266
00:25:50,368 --> 00:25:54,096
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) is saying that I am promise you, not to throw you into the destruction.

267
00:25:55,179 --> 00:26:02,510
He would only send out the army, if there was sufficient reconnaissance done

268
00:26:02,934 --> 00:26:06,234
and if there is not great risk and there is not great risk.

269
00:26:09,289 --> 00:26:11,936
So, there is difference between Defensive Jihad(جهاد) and Offensive Jihad(جهاد).

270
00:26:11,960 --> 00:26:15,837
In Defensive Jihad(جهاد), the Muslims takes greater risk

271
00:26:16,861 --> 00:26:22,361
and they sacrifice their lives and their wealth and their family.

272
00:26:23,269 --> 00:26:27,191
But when we are talking about Offensive Jihad(جهاد), which is for the sake of Daw'ah(دعوة)

273
00:26:29,492 --> 00:26:31,480
the risk that, they take is less.

274
00:26:32,614 --> 00:26:36,714
And their safety is taken into consideration by the Khulafah(خلفاء),

275
00:26:37,668 --> 00:26:40,492
that was something that Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) instituted

276
00:26:40,516 --> 00:26:46,293
and it was something also that we find with Umar Bin Abdul-Aziz رضي الله عنه he recalled the army

277
00:26:46,333 --> 00:26:48,939
that was laying siege on Constantinople(قسطنطنية)

278
00:26:49,163 --> 00:26:51,163
because he said, that the Muslims are dying.

279
00:26:58,292 --> 00:27:05,390
Number five: The role of the leader is to protect the people not to protect himself.

280
00:27:06,981 --> 00:27:10,579
Now, the leaders they are concerned about their personal safety,

281
00:27:10,627 --> 00:27:11,816
they don’t care about the Ummah(امة).

282
00:27:11,856 --> 00:27:12,899
Let the Ummah(امة) die!

283
00:27:14,136 --> 00:27:19,174
As long as I am safe, I am going to use the entire army and police force to protect myself

284
00:27:20,789 --> 00:27:25,377
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was concerned about the safety of the Ummah(امة).

285
00:27:26,476 --> 00:27:28,642
So, he said, I am not going to throw you in destruction.

286
00:27:28,699 --> 00:27:31,040
 I am going to take care of you, I am going to take care of your families.

287
00:27:31,636 --> 00:27:34,764
While, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) would go around without any security guards.

288
00:27:36,268 --> 00:27:40,570
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) did not have even one bodyguard to accompany him

289
00:27:41,247 --> 00:27:45,145
but he use to pay a lot of attention to the security of Muslims.

290
00:27:48,459 --> 00:27:50,180
In fact, in one of his letter, he said;

291
00:27:50,363 --> 00:27:57,612
You do not sent out reconnaissance mission unless they are properly secured and defended.

292
00:28:03,153 --> 00:28:04,128
Number six;

293
00:28:06,374 --> 00:28:09,894
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) is telling his army

294
00:28:10,972 --> 00:28:16,357
in your absence I will be the father to your children and care taker of your wives.

295
00:28:18,101 --> 00:28:25,663
Just think about how much psychological comfort that would give to a soldier when he is fighting.

296
00:28:26,976 --> 00:28:32,054
When he is in the front line, he will realize that if something happens to him,

297
00:28:32,629 --> 00:28:34,195
my family would be taken care of.

298
00:28:35,834 --> 00:28:39,682
The Khalifah(خليفه) would be their father, he will be there for them.

299
00:28:40,559 --> 00:28:44,517
So, this motivates the army, it’s a morale boost for them

300
00:28:46,838 --> 00:28:50,468
and this is the concerned that the leader should have for his people.

301
00:28:50,988 --> 00:28:52,986
And that’s why? Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

302
00:28:53,950 --> 00:28:56,038
مَا مِنْ نَبِيْ إِلَّا وَرَعِى الْغَنَمْ

303
00:28:56,780 --> 00:29:01,648
"That every Prophet has been a shepherd of sheep".

304
00:29:03,216 --> 00:29:05,498
They said: "what about you, Rasool Allah ﷺ ?" He said: Even me!

305
00:29:06,637 --> 00:29:10,175
How come all of the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء) were shepherds of sheep? Specifically sheep.

306
00:29:11,004 --> 00:29:15,172
because a shepherd of sheep is dealing with a weak animals,

307
00:29:15,532 --> 00:29:18,132
these are not camels these are sheep

308
00:29:18,676 --> 00:29:20,894
see the camel is an arrogant proud animal

309
00:29:21,248 --> 00:29:23,992
but the sheep are weak and they are vulnerable

310
00:29:24,335 --> 00:29:28,923
they could be attacked at any moment, by a wolf or a wild animal.

311
00:29:31,165 --> 00:29:41,493
So, the shepherd learns responsibility and is always guarding his flock.

312
00:29:42,402 --> 00:29:47,140
And the shepherd has a lot of mercy towards these weak animals.

313
00:29:47,961 --> 00:29:52,674
So, that is the training for the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء), so when they start giving Daw'ah(دعوة) to the people

314
00:29:53,578 --> 00:29:55,990
they carry on those characteristics with them.

315
00:29:57,225 --> 00:30:01,662
They see themselves as responsible for the security of their followers,

316
00:30:02,058 --> 00:30:07,658
they see themselves as care takers of their followers.

317
00:30:09,864 --> 00:30:17,142
And a shepherd since he is standing, has a vantage point, that the sheep do not have.

318
00:30:18,035 --> 00:30:23,482
The shepherd is the first to see danger approaching, but the sheep cannot see that coming.

319
00:30:24,772 --> 00:30:31,200
So, the Nabi(نَبِي) of Allah has that ability to see the danger when it's on its way before his followers.

320
00:30:31,680 --> 00:30:33,159
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying;

321
00:30:33,461 --> 00:30:37,409
The analogy of me and you is like somebody who's sitting next to the bonfire.

322
00:30:37,633 --> 00:30:41,821
And all of these flying insects are trying to jump into the fire,

323
00:30:42,245 --> 00:30:44,845
thinking that it’s a light and they don’t know that it will burn them.

324
00:30:45,262 --> 00:30:50,190
And I am pulling you away from fire while you are forcing yourselves into it.

325
00:30:52,344 --> 00:30:53,615
وَأَنْتُمْ تَقَّحْمُوْنَ فِيْهَا

326
00:30:53,639 --> 00:30:56,491
Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying I want to save you from the fire

327
00:30:57,131 --> 00:30:59,223
and you don’t know that you are a heading towards it.

328
00:31:01,023 --> 00:31:06,955
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) is now treating the Ummah(امة) as if he is the shepherd, caring for them.

329
00:31:09,513 --> 00:31:11,167
AN ISSUE RELATING TO BAY'AH(بيعة):

330
00:31:12,210 --> 00:31:13,208
Number one:

331
00:31:14,054 --> 00:31:18,674
The Bay’ah(بيعة) that was given to the Khulafah(خُلَافَاء) was given only by the people of Madina.

332
00:31:19,998 --> 00:31:21,741
It wasn’t given by everybody.

333
00:31:21,820 --> 00:31:27,073
As long as the people of Madina gave Bay’ah(بيعة) to the Khalifah(خليفه) that was seen as sufficient.

334
00:31:27,870 --> 00:31:33,488
They didn’t get the Bay’ah(بيعة) from each and every Muslim living in the Khilafah(خِلَافَه)

335
00:31:33,795 --> 00:31:35,253
because it is impossible to do that.

336
00:31:37,360 --> 00:31:38,923
It would take months and months

337
00:31:39,431 --> 00:31:43,579
if they are going to solicit Bay’ah(بيعة) from each and every individual living in Islamic Khilafah(خِلَافَه).

338
00:31:44,005 --> 00:31:47,533
So, as long as the people of Madina gave Bay’ah(بيعة) that was seen as sufficient

339
00:31:48,013 --> 00:31:50,180
and after that all of the people follow.

340
00:31:51,062 --> 00:31:52,120
So, Al-Madina had

341
00:31:52,160 --> 00:31:53,096
اَهْلُ الْحَلِّ وَالْعَقْدَ

342
00:31:53,144 --> 00:31:55,785
It had the people, who make the decision.

343
00:31:56,158 --> 00:31:56,601
That’s number one.

344
00:31:56,665 --> 00:31:57,310
2. Number two:

345
00:31:58,453 --> 00:32:04,221
We don’t find it anywhere in our old references that, they took Bay’ah(بيعة) from women

346
00:32:05,106 --> 00:32:07,112
It was only the men, who were giving the Bay’ah(بيعة)

347
00:32:07,695 --> 00:32:11,961
women never gave Bay’ah(بيعة) to Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) or Umar(عُمَر) or Uthman(عثمان) or Ali(علي)

348
00:32:12,226 --> 00:32:14,043
or any of the Khulfah(خلافاء) after that.

349
00:32:15,587 --> 00:32:19,920
And that was seen as a natural thing to the extent

350
00:32:19,960 --> 00:32:25,199
that none of our classical scholars ever talked about that issue in their books of Fiqh(فقه).

351
00:32:27,028 --> 00:32:31,766
It was seen as natural or normal for the men to give the Bay’ah(بيعة)

352
00:32:32,519 --> 00:32:34,586
and the women not to give the Bay’ah(بيعة).

353
00:32:35,867 --> 00:32:38,998
But on the other hand, there is nothing in Qur’an or Sunnah(سنة) that says

354
00:32:39,077 --> 00:32:40,951
that the women are not allowed to give Baiy’ah(بيعة).

355
00:32:42,075 --> 00:32:43,580
So, the issue is left open.

356
00:32:43,985 --> 00:32:45,609
Women never gave Bay’ah(بيعة) before

357
00:32:45,689 --> 00:32:51,505
however, there is nothing in Qur’an or Sunnah(سنة) that prohibits them from giving Baiy’ah(بيعة).

358
00:32:51,859 --> 00:32:56,905
And this is like many of the other issues that relate to politics.

359
00:32:57,956 --> 00:33:01,454
The general guide lines were given in Qur’an and Sunnah(سنة)

360
00:33:01,823 --> 00:33:07,261
but the details were left open for the people to formulate according to the need of their times.

361
00:33:08,432 --> 00:33:12,609
Even when it came to the appointment of the Khalifah(خليفه), we find that it happened in different ways

362
00:33:13,015 --> 00:33:19,783
Rasool Allah ﷺ did not appoint anyone even though he gave many implicit indications

363
00:33:20,107 --> 00:33:21,907
 that Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) should be the Khalifah(خليفه).

364
00:33:22,292 --> 00:33:23,713
He was the Imam(اِمَام) of Salah(صلاة).

365
00:33:23,937 --> 00:33:25,437
He was Ameer(امير) on Hajj(حَجْ).

366
00:33:26,758 --> 00:33:29,426
When women came to Rasool Allah ﷺ he said,

367
00:33:29,957 --> 00:33:34,035
She asked for something from Rasool Allahﷺ told her to come later

368
00:33:34,259 --> 00:33:38,030
she said: What if I don’t find you? He said: "Go to Abu Bakr(ابو بكر)"

369
00:33:39,318 --> 00:33:42,456
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling this woman that if you don’t find me

370
00:33:43,049 --> 00:33:45,605
the next in line is Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه.

371
00:33:46,729 --> 00:33:49,355
While Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) appointed Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) specifically.

372
00:33:49,597 --> 00:33:53,370
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) appointed a council of six to choose.

373
00:33:54,440 --> 00:33:56,107
So, it was done in different ways.

374
00:33:57,467 --> 00:33:59,075
The general guidelines are

375
00:33:59,258 --> 00:34:00,544
Al-Adl(العدل) justice,

376
00:34:00,790 --> 00:34:02,925
Shoora(شورى) consultation

377
00:34:03,204 --> 00:34:04,957
Baiy’ah(بيعة) giving pledge of allegiance

378
00:34:05,317 --> 00:34:12,935
but other areas are left open for the Mujtahideen(مجتهدين) to decide according to the needs of the time.

379
00:34:15,977 --> 00:34:20,625
Now, women were consulted in terms of Shoora(شورى), women are consulted

380
00:34:21,470 --> 00:34:27,378
it is just the Baiy’ah(بيعة) that, they didn’t give the Baiy’ah(بيعة) to Khulafah(خلافاء)

381
00:34:28,001 --> 00:34:32,892
They did however, give Bay’ah(بيعة) to Rasool Allah ﷺ which was the Baiy’ah(بيعة) Of Islam.

382
00:34:41,024 --> 00:34:43,943
WE WILL TALK ABOUT THE GOVERNMENT OF UMAR IBN KHATTAB رضي الله عنه.

383
00:34:48,816 --> 00:34:52,294
Number one: Shoora(شورى) it was a government of Shoora(شورى).

384
00:34:53,385 --> 00:34:54,685
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

385
00:34:55,463 --> 00:34:58,042
فَبِمَا رَحْمَةٍ مِنَ اللَّهِ لِنْتَ لَهُمْ

386
00:34:58,806 --> 00:35:02,462
وَلَوْ كُنْتَ فَظًّا غَلِيظَ الْقَلْبِ لَانْفَضُّوا مِنْ حَوْلِكَ

387
00:35:03,362 --> 00:35:05,997
فَاعْفُ عَنْهُمْ وَاسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ وَشَاوِرْهُمْ فِي الْأَمْرِ

388
00:35:06,581 --> 00:35:11,649
فَإِذَا عَزَمْتَ فَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَى اللَّهِ ۚ إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُحِبُّ الْمُتَوَكِّلِينَ۝

389
00:35:13,851 --> 00:35:18,499
"It is part of the mercy of Allah that you do deal gently with them

390
00:35:19,257 --> 00:35:25,806
where if you were severe or harsh hearted, they would have broken away from about you.

391
00:35:26,405 --> 00:35:30,695
So, pass over their faults and ask for Allah’s forgiveness for them

392
00:35:31,215 --> 00:35:34,923
and consult them in their affairs.

393
00:35:35,729 --> 00:35:39,037
Then when you have taken a decision put your trust in Allah

394
00:35:39,355 --> 00:35:42,114
for Allah love those who put their trust in Him."

395
00:35:42,438 --> 00:35:44,329
Al-Imran(ألعمران) verse 159.

396
00:35:45,861 --> 00:35:46,949
Umar Ibn Khattab(عمرإبن ألخطاب) said;

397
00:35:47,038 --> 00:35:50,676
لَا خَيْرَ فِيْ اَمْرٍاُ بْرِ مَا مِنْ غَيْرِ شُوْرى

398
00:35:51,299 --> 00:35:55,657
There is no good in an affair, that was decided without consultation.

399
00:35:56,677 --> 00:35:57,881
There is no Barakah(بركة) in it.

400
00:36:00,400 --> 00:36:04,060
So, if you want to have Barakah(بركة) in your affairs make Shoora(شورى)

401
00:36:05,872 --> 00:36:06,860
He also says;

402
00:36:07,268 --> 00:36:10,746
شَاوِرْ فِيْ أَمْرِكَ مَنْ يَخَافُ الله تَعَالى

403
00:36:11,734 --> 00:36:15,309
Consult in your affairs the ones, who fear Allah.

404
00:36:18,162 --> 00:36:21,450
And this is an important teaching,

405
00:36:23,998 --> 00:36:27,263
you need to consult the people of Taqwa(تقوي) the people of righteousness.

406
00:36:28,605 --> 00:36:30,963
If you consult a Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ), he will not do you any good.

407
00:36:32,856 --> 00:36:37,070
It doesn’t say that you go and make a Shoora(شورى) with everyone including Iblees(ابليس) you ask him for his opinions.

408
00:36:37,780 --> 00:36:40,848
and it also means that you don’t go and ask the opinion of his followers.

409
00:36:42,574 --> 00:36:48,162
So, you don’t go around asking for advice from people,

410
00:36:48,796 --> 00:36:52,464
who do not have the concern for the religion of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

411
00:36:53,160 --> 00:36:57,022
You need to seek the Shoora(شورى) from the people who have Taqwa(تقوى) of Allah

412
00:36:58,510 --> 00:37:01,948
and they also need to be experts in that particular area that you are asking them.

413
00:37:03,135 --> 00:37:06,293
Not everybody who has Taqwa(تقوى) of Allahعَزّوجَلّ knows about everything

414
00:37:08,027 --> 00:37:12,990
So, when you seek Shoora(شورى), consultation

415
00:37:14,160 --> 00:37:19,198
you look for Taqwa(تقوى) and you also look for competence in that particular area.

416
00:37:19,309 --> 00:37:20,709
They have to know what they are talking about?

417
00:37:22,099 --> 00:37:30,767
So, these two qualities are the two elements that are needed when you are looking for advice.

418
00:37:32,342 --> 00:37:36,606
There are many people, who have understanding but they don’t have Taqwa(تقوى)

419
00:37:36,816 --> 00:37:39,520
and there are many people of Taqwa(تقوى) but they don’t have the understanding.

420
00:37:40,960 --> 00:37:44,290
So, you have to go to the right people and ask them for Shoora(شورى).

421
00:37:49,254 --> 00:37:52,311
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) not only would he make Shoora(شورى)

422
00:37:52,351 --> 00:37:56,859
but he would make sure that, his governors, and generals would make Shoora(شورى).

423
00:37:57,084 --> 00:38:03,647
For example, when he appointed Abi Obaid Thaqafi(اَبِي عُبَيْداَلثَّقَفِيْ) to lead an army he said;

424
00:38:03,672 --> 00:38:08,881
اِسْمَعْ وَاَطَعْ مِنْ اَصْحَابِيْ اَنَّبِيِّ  صلى الله عليه وسلم وَأَشْرِكْمْ فِيْ الْأَمْرِيْ

425
00:38:09,243 --> 00:38:11,197
خَاصَةً مِّنْ كَانَ مِنْهُمْ مِنْ اَهْلِ بَدْرََ

426
00:38:11,521 --> 00:38:15,459
"He told him, listen and obey to the Companions of Rasool Allah ﷺ

427
00:38:15,483 --> 00:38:17,551
because he wasn’t Companion, he was a Taba’ee(تابعي),

428
00:38:17,808 --> 00:38:21,062
he said listen and obey to the companions of Rasool Allah ﷺ

429
00:38:21,360 --> 00:38:23,078
especially those who have attended Badr(بدر)."

430
00:38:25,582 --> 00:38:31,565
And he told Utbah Bin Ghazwan(عتبه ابن غزوان), who he also appointed as an army general,

431
00:38:31,719 --> 00:38:35,383
he told him, I have written a letter to Abi Al-Ala Hadrami(ابو الاعلى حضرمى)

432
00:38:36,188 --> 00:38:40,070
to send with you ‘Arfajah Ibn Harshama(عرفجه ابن هرشمه),

433
00:38:40,368 --> 00:38:45,699
وَهُوَ ذُوْا مُجَاهَدَةْ لِلْعَدُّوْ وَمُكَايَدَتَهْ فَإِذَا قَدِمَ عَلَيْكَ فَاسْتَشِرْهُ وَقَرِّبْهُُ

434
00:38:46,203 --> 00:38:50,046
"I told Abu Al-Ala Hadrami(ابو الاعلى حضرمى) to send with you this man Arfajah(عرفجه)

435
00:38:50,415 --> 00:38:55,613
and Umar(عُمَر) told him this man is good, in his fighting the enemy and their plans."

436
00:38:56,053 --> 00:38:59,301
He knows how to fight the enemy and to fight the plans of the enemy.

437
00:38:59,940 --> 00:39:01,682
So, he needs to be with you and he said;

438
00:39:02,007 --> 00:39:02,678
اسْتَشِرْهُ

439
00:39:03,285 --> 00:39:07,203
"Seek his advice and make him close to you, Waqraba'a(وقربه).

440
00:39:10,778 --> 00:39:17,056
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) for example, he placed a travel ban on the senior Sahabah(صحابه),

441
00:39:17,524 --> 00:39:19,183
 he told them you are not allowed to leave the Madina

442
00:39:21,000 --> 00:39:22,995
You know Umar(عُمَر) have some strict rules.

443
00:39:24,655 --> 00:39:29,631
He told all of these senior Sahabah(صحابه), you are not allowed to leave Madina, you have to stick to me here.

444
00:39:29,917 --> 00:39:32,789
One reason was he wanted them to be his Shoora(شورى) Council

445
00:39:33,285 --> 00:39:42,161
another reason was Umar(عُمَر) was afraid that if these senior men spread around

446
00:39:44,075 --> 00:39:48,343
that could be a reason for contention and divisions among the Muslims.

447
00:39:48,774 --> 00:39:52,032
Because all of these men are strong leaders

448
00:39:53,750 --> 00:39:56,428
so people are going to coming around them

449
00:39:57,099 --> 00:40:00,555
and then you will have various points of influence among the Ummah(امة).

450
00:40:01,679 --> 00:40:05,697
And he was afraid that everyone of these men would lead the people in different direction

451
00:40:06,050 --> 00:40:08,441
so he wanted to make sure that they are under his watchful eye.

452
00:40:10,715 --> 00:40:12,723
So, he told them that you have to stick with me here in Madina

453
00:40:16,195 --> 00:40:18,426
SOME OF HIS CLOSE ADVISORS,

454
00:40:18,589 --> 00:40:22,937
Al-Abbas Bin Abdul-Muttalib(العباس ابن عبدالمطلب) the uncle of Rasool Allah ﷺ and his son Abdullah(عبدالله)

455
00:40:24,353 --> 00:40:27,681
Now Abdullah(عبدالله) was young, he is very young.

456
00:40:29,463 --> 00:40:34,001
Abdullah Ibn Abbas(عبدالله ابن عباس) was thirteen years old when Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away.

457
00:40:35,299 --> 00:40:40,847
So, here we are talking about someone who was in his early twenties

458
00:40:42,311 --> 00:40:46,589
And you would always find him, next to Umar(عُمَر).

459
00:40:47,397 --> 00:40:49,412
He would accompany him, where ever Umar(عُمَر) would go.

460
00:40:50,076 --> 00:40:53,604
So some of the elder Sahabah(صحابه) were wondering how come?

461
00:40:54,668 --> 00:40:59,968
This young man was sitting on this Shoora(شورى) body.

462
00:41:02,857 --> 00:41:07,302
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) wanted them to know the reason.

463
00:41:07,596 --> 00:41:14,698
So, he asked him, he said: "Tell me what's the meaning of;

464
00:41:16,972 --> 00:41:25,587
إِذَا جَاءَ نَصْرُ اللَّهِ وَالْفَتْحُ ۝ وَرَأَيْتَ النَّاسَ يَدْخُلُونَ فِي دِينِ اللَّهِ أَفْوَاجًا ۝ فَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ وَاسْتَغْفِرْهُ إِنَّهُ كَانَ تَوَّابًا۝

465
00:41:26,552 --> 00:41:31,866
"When the victory of Allah approaches and people enter into Islam in multitudes

466
00:41:32,212 --> 00:41:36,150
then ask Allah for forgiveness because Allah is Forgiving and Merciful."

467
00:41:36,574 --> 00:41:38,751
what does this Surah(سورة) mean?

468
00:41:39,620 --> 00:41:42,578
So, the Sahabah(صحابه) mentioned some few different views

469
00:41:42,797 --> 00:41:45,035
and then he asked Ibn Abbas(ابن عباس) what does it mean?

470
00:41:45,636 --> 00:41:49,752
He said: "This Surah(سورة) is the obituary of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

471
00:41:50,185 --> 00:41:52,263
it was telling him that your death is near.

472
00:41:53,577 --> 00:41:56,635
Because when you finish a deed Allah tells you to ask for forgiveness.

473
00:41:57,115 --> 00:42:00,653
So, since Allahعَزّوجَلّ is telling Muhammadﷺ to ask Allah for forgiveness,

474
00:42:01,017 --> 00:42:03,617
it means that he has completed his mission.

475
00:42:05,049 --> 00:42:07,547
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said, that’s why Ibn Abbas(ابن عباس) is with me.

476
00:42:10,226 --> 00:42:11,855
He was the only one, who knew the answer.

477
00:42:14,830 --> 00:42:19,424
Some of his advisors are, Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) and Abdur Rahman Ibn Aauf(عبدالرحمن ابن عوف),

478
00:42:19,448 --> 00:42:24,216
and Ali Ibn Abi Talib رضي الله عنه, and Ubae Ibn Ka'ab(ابيئ بن كعب), scholar of Quran

479
00:42:24,241 --> 00:42:26,577
Zayd Ibn Thabit(زيد ابن ثابت), the one, who compiled Al-Mus'haf(المصحف).

480
00:42:27,009 --> 00:42:30,676
These were the close advisor of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه.

481
00:42:32,092 --> 00:42:35,330
His government, was a government of justice and equality.

482
00:42:37,057 --> 00:42:45,288
Imam Malik(امام مالك) says that, a Jew and a Muslim came to Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) to solve a dispute

483
00:42:45,522 --> 00:42:47,263
that happened between them.

484
00:42:48,161 --> 00:42:56,601
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) is Judgment was for the Jew against the Muslim.

485
00:42:58,521 --> 00:43:05,061
 When the Jew walked out he said: "In the name of Allah, you are ruling with Justice.

486
00:43:06,699 --> 00:43:07,815
لَقَدْ قَضَيْتَ بِالْحَقّ

487
00:43:07,985 --> 00:43:14,672
This is Al-Haq(الحق), so he judged for a Jew, over a Muslim.

488
00:43:19,278 --> 00:43:22,686
And he was very strict when it comes to his governors.

489
00:43:23,094 --> 00:43:26,552
He wanted to make sure that they would apply, Adl(عدل).

490
00:43:29,466 --> 00:43:34,014
Every year he would meet with the subjects in Hajj(حَجْ).

491
00:43:35,256 --> 00:43:37,417
And he would ask them about their governors.

492
00:43:38,092 --> 00:43:40,153
So, he gave a Khutba(خطبة) once he said;

493
00:43:40,193 --> 00:43:44,474
إِنِّيْ لَمْ اَبْعَثْ عُمَّالِيْ عَلَيْكُمْ لِيُصِيْبُوْا مِنْ أَبْشَارِكُمْ

494
00:43:44,938 --> 00:43:50,594
وَلَا مِنْ اَمْوَالِكُمْ وَإِنَّمَا بَعَثْتَ هُمْ لِيَحْجِزُوْا بَيْنَكُمْ

495
00:43:50,898 --> 00:43:56,238
وَلِيَقْسِمُوْا فَيْءَ كُمْ بَيْنَكُمْ فَمَنْ فَعَلَ فُعِلَ بِهِ غَيْرَ ذَلِكْ فَلْيَقُمْ

496
00:43:56,524 --> 00:44:03,815
He said: I did not send my governors to flog you and to take away your wealth

497
00:44:04,315 --> 00:44:08,611
 but I sent them to distribute your wealth between you fairly

498
00:44:09,032 --> 00:44:12,544
and to solve your disputes.

499
00:44:13,142 --> 00:44:15,172
So, the governors are there to serve you

500
00:44:16,604 --> 00:44:20,225
And if anything other than that happens to you let me know.

501
00:44:21,992 --> 00:44:27,235
So, one man stood up and said; "Your governor whipped me a hundred lashes."

502
00:44:28,959 --> 00:44:31,357
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) asked the governor, why did he do it?

503
00:44:31,381 --> 00:44:33,081
He didn’t get the satisfactory answer

504
00:44:33,712 --> 00:44:38,940
he told this subject to go and lash the governor.

505
00:44:40,055 --> 00:44:41,515
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عمرو بن العاص) stood up and said;

506
00:44:41,555 --> 00:44:43,952
"O Ameerul Mo’mineen(امير المؤمنين) what you are doing is dangerous

507
00:44:45,841 --> 00:44:55,565
if you start this, the news of it will spread and it would be a frequent occurrence of people complaining against their governors

508
00:44:57,795 --> 00:44:59,943
and it would become a Sunnah(سنة) after you.

509
00:45:02,383 --> 00:45:07,280
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: "Retribution must be paid to this man."

510
00:45:07,792 --> 00:45:14,330
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) said: And this is something that Rasool Allah ﷺ used to do,

511
00:45:15,009 --> 00:45:17,328
you ask me to change the Sunnah(سنة) of Rasool Allah ﷺ?

512
00:45:18,248 --> 00:45:19,511
Amr Bin Al-Aas(عمرو بن العاص) said;

513
00:45:19,551 --> 00:45:23,155
O Ameer-Ul-Mo'mineen(امير المؤمنين) let us settle the affair with the man peacefully.

514
00:45:24,160 --> 00:45:27,535
He goes to the man and negotiates with him a settlement

515
00:45:28,008 --> 00:45:36,116
he agrees that he would be paid two dinars for every one whipping.

516
00:45:36,937 --> 00:45:41,559
So, we're talking about two hundred Dinars(دينار), which is a large amount of money.

517
00:45:41,968 --> 00:45:44,002
But Amr Bin Al-Aas(عمرو بن العاص) wanted to settle it peacefully

518
00:45:44,066 --> 00:45:48,202
because he didn’t want all of the governors to be lashed after that.

519
00:45:48,258 --> 00:45:50,373
Because he was one of them, he is one of the governors.

520
00:45:57,587 --> 00:46:02,034
In fact one incidence that happened with Amr Bin Al-Aas(عمرو بن العاص) when he was the governor in Egypt.

521
00:46:02,729 --> 00:46:10,137
His son got involved in a racing competition with an Egyptian.

522
00:46:11,712 --> 00:46:13,012
So, the Egyptian won.

523
00:46:13,879 --> 00:46:16,161
 The son of  Amr Bin Al-Aas(عمرو بن العاص) was upset and angry

524
00:46:16,463 --> 00:46:20,611
so he start beating up this man, why did you win?

525
00:46:23,830 --> 00:46:35,813
